<section class="prose">
  <h1>Support Eleven</h1>

  <p id="thanks" hidden>
    <strong>Thank you.</strong> Your donation landed and it means a lot —
    it goes straight to work. That&rsquo;s the whole ceremony; there is no
    mailing list.
  </p>

  <h2>There&rsquo;s no funding</h2>
  <p>
    Eleven has no investors, no ad money, and no growth team. So far,
    it&rsquo;s been independently funded by <a href="http://ti.to">Team
    Tito</a>, and <a href="https://lazyatom.com">James Adam</a> and
    hasn&rsquo;t <a href="https://status.elevenmessenger.com/books.html">cost
    too much</a>. It&rsquo;s a project in defiance of big tech and of
    over-complexity in software distribution — proof that a small team can
    build top-tier, secure software and hand it to people simply: starting
    with affordable &ldquo;cloud&rdquo; hosting, all the way to a single
    binary you can host yourself. There&rsquo;s no tracking, no dark
    patterns. It&rsquo;s an experiment in rethinking how software is
    produced, operated and distributed.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you support those ideas, you can back us directly. We&rsquo;ll
    plough every donation into creating a software organisation that acts in
    a verifiably and independently auditable way, that promotes a commitment
    to a new bar in standards for security, privacy, ownership, respect,
    openness, and transparency.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we do take on any investment money, it will be under
    <a href="https://status.elevenmessenger.com/funding.html">open terms and
    a transparent returns model</a>, in line with a commitment to
    <a href="https://status.elevenmessenger.com/books.html">open ledger
    books</a>, and
    <a href="https://status.elevenmessenger.com/economics.html">open unit
    economics</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Bear in mind</h2>
  <p>
    Eleven isn&rsquo;t a charity. It&rsquo;s not even a company yet. A
    donation buys nothing, promises nothing, and isn&rsquo;t tax-deductible.
    It&rsquo;s just voting with your wallet to add fuel to the fire against
    the malfeasance of a generation of software &ldquo;pioneers&rdquo; who
    have treated data like oil and built their own extraction industry
    around it.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you can&rsquo;t afford to donate: <strong>DO NOT DONATE.</strong>
    Paul and James have enough. Only throw money at us if you have way more
    than you need and you like popcorn.
  </p>

  <h2>What&rsquo;s the catch?</h2>
  <p>
    The catch is this is an AI-driven project.
  </p>
  <p>
    The ideas behind Eleven are the culmination of years of disillusionment
    accrued over thousands of paper cuts and a treadmill of software being
    released with good intentions and turning shit when the economic
    interests of the creators stopped aligning with the interests of the
    customers.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is a project that wouldn&rsquo;t exist without AI. The manner in
    which LLMs have been trained on stolen knowledge is reprehensible. The
    lies, the hype, the shady tactics, the ecological impact, everything.
    But the technology allows for uncompromising, rapid software development
    at a rate never seen before, and a rapid interaction cycle of asking:
    &ldquo;but what if we did it this way?&rdquo;.
  </p>
  <p>
    Eleven is an attempt to show people who use AI flippantly to fart out
    slop that maybe, just maybe, it can also be used to craft new, better
    things, and rather than just dream about better technology built for
    humans, to just make it.
  </p>

  <h2>Donate</h2>
  <div class="donate-row">
    <button class="btn btn-ghost donate-amt" data-minor="111100">€1,111</button>
    <button class="btn btn-ghost donate-amt" data-minor="1111100">€11,111</button>
    <button class="btn btn-ghost donate-amt" data-minor="11111100">€111,111</button>
  </div>
  <form id="donate-custom" class="donate-custom">
    <label for="donate-amount">Or pick your own amount</label>
    <div class="donate-row">
      <select id="donate-cur" aria-label="Currency">
        <option value="eur" selected>€ EUR</option>
        <option value="usd">$ USD</option>
        <option value="gbp">£ GBP</option>
      </select>
      <input id="donate-amount" type="number" min="1111" step="0.01" placeholder="1111.00"
             inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="donate-note" />
      <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Donate</button>
    </div>
  </form>
  <p class="fine" id="donate-note">
    Pay what you want, from €1,111. Payment runs on Stripe&rsquo;s hosted
    page; we never see your card.
  </p>
  <p class="fine" id="donate-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
</section>

<style>
  /* 🤖 One control height across the whole form — the presets, the currency
     select, the amount field, and the button all sit on the same line-height
     so nothing reads as an afterthought. Fields match the site's pill
     language (999px, 1.5px borders) without pretending to be buttons. */
  .donate-row { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: stretch; }
  .donate-row > * { min-height: 2.9rem; }
  .donate-amt { min-width: 6.5rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .donate-custom { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .donate-custom label { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .donate-custom select,
  .donate-custom input {
    font: inherit;
    color: inherit;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1.5px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.55rem 1.1rem;
  }
  .donate-custom select { padding-right: 0.9rem; }
  .donate-custom input { width: 8.5rem; }
  /* the number spinners fight the pill shape — the keyboard still steps */
  .donate-custom input::-webkit-outer-spin-button,
  .donate-custom input::-webkit-inner-spin-button { -webkit-appearance: none; margin: 0; }
  .donate-custom input[type="number"] { -moz-appearance: textfield; appearance: textfield; }
</style>

<script type="module">
  // 🤖 Same shape as the Enterprise page: the static site has no backend, so
  // checkout mints on the cloud service (CORS-scoped to this origin).
  const CHECKOUT_URL = "https://cloud.elevenmessenger.com/api/donate/checkout";
  const err = document.getElementById("donate-error");
  if (new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("thanks") === "1") {
    document.getElementById("thanks").hidden = false;
  }
  async function donate(amountMinor, currency) {
    err.hidden = true;
    try {
      const resp = await fetch(CHECKOUT_URL, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: JSON.stringify({ amount_minor: amountMinor, currency }),
      });
      const body = await resp.json();
      if (!resp.ok || !body.url) throw new Error(body.message || "checkout failed");
      location.href = body.url;
    } catch (e) {
      err.textContent = "Couldn’t start the checkout — " + e.message + ". Please try again.";
      err.hidden = false;
    }
  }
  for (const b of document.querySelectorAll(".donate-amt")) {
    b.addEventListener("click", () => donate(Number(b.dataset.minor), "eur"));
  }
  document.getElementById("donate-custom").addEventListener("submit", (ev) => {
    ev.preventDefault();
    const v = Number(document.getElementById("donate-amount").value);
    if (!Number.isFinite(v) || v < 1111) {
      err.textContent = "Donations start at 1,111 — see Bear in mind above.";
      err.hidden = false;
      return;
    }
    donate(Math.round(v * 100), document.getElementById("donate-cur").value);
  });
</script>
